            "rubricHtml": "<p>Questions 21–26</p>",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "questions": [
              {
                "number": 21,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;Daniel mentions the research about walking and creativity to Katie because",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "she has read it too."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "what she says reminds him of it."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "he thinks she might like to do similar research."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 22,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;In the experiments, researchers compared participants' creativity when walking and when",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "sitting."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "running."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "listening to music."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 23,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;Daniel says that in each experiment, there was a different",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "type of control group."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "pattern of activities."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "way of selecting participants."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 24,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;Daniel thinks the experiment with words is",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "biased in favour of certain people."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "a good indicator of creativity."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "open to personal interpretation."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 25,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;What is Katie and Daniel's attitude to the experiment on focused thinking?",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "they are doubtful about its aims."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "they are confused by its methods."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "they are cautious about its conclusions."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 26,
                "textHtml": "&nbsp;Katie thinks that the best way forward is to consider",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "whether other types of exercise affect creativity."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "the cause of the improvement in creativity."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "how the results can be applied to creativity in real life."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
